# Code Signing Certificate Placeholder
# 
# To enable code signing for Windows builds:
# 1. Obtain a valid code signing certificate (PFX format)
# 2. Save it as installer-assets/cert.pfx
# 3. Set CERTIFICATE_PASSWORD environment variable with the certificate password
# 4. electron-builder will automatically sign the Windows installer
#
# Recommended certificate providers:
# - DigiCert (https://www.digicert.com)
# - Sectigo (https://sectigo.com)
# - Comodo (https://comodo.com)
# - GlobalSign (https://www.globalsign.com)
#
# For development/testing, you can use a self-signed certificate:
# openssl req -x509 -newkey rsa:4096 -keyout key.pem -out cert.crt -days 365 -nodes
# openssl pkcs12 -export -out cert.pfx -inkey key.pem -in cert.crt
#
# Note: Windows SmartScreen requires certificates from trusted CAs.
# Self-signed certificates will trigger SmartScreen warnings.
